1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:01,840
It's freezing outside.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,757
So how can that air heat your home?

3
00:00:04,287 --> 00:00:06,287
Even freezing air holds heat.

4
00:00:06,407 --> 00:00:09,809
Zero Celsius is still
far above absolute zero.

5
00:00:10,549 --> 00:00:12,929
A heat pump moves that heat indoors,

6
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:15,292
with refrigerant circling a sealed loop.

7
00:00:15,962 --> 00:00:18,356
Outside, refrigerant
colder than the air

8
00:00:18,356 --> 00:00:21,131
soaks up its heat
and boils into a gas.

9
00:00:21,691 --> 00:00:23,551
A compressor squeezes the gas,

10
00:00:23,551 --> 00:00:25,260
and its temperature shoots up.

11
00:00:25,791 --> 00:00:28,401
Indoors, the hot gas
releases that heat

12
00:00:28,401 --> 00:00:31,131
into your home and
condenses to a liquid.

13
00:00:31,661 --> 00:00:33,981
An expansion valve drops the pressure,

14
00:00:33,981 --> 00:00:35,461
the liquid goes cold,

15
00:00:35,461 --> 00:00:36,756
and the loop repeats.

16
00:00:37,516 --> 00:00:39,436
Moving heat beats making it.

17
00:00:39,496 --> 00:00:42,600
You usually get more heat
out than electricity in.
